.TH DCLIENT 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
dclient \- send NNTP commands to a news server and print the replies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dclient
[
.B \-f
.I file
]
[
.B \-p
.I port
]
[
.B \-v
]
[
.B \-V
]
.I host
[
.I command
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dclient
connects to the NNTP server on
.I host
(port 119 by default), sends a command and writes the reply to standard
output, then sends QUIT.  The command is one argument, so quote a command
with arguments.  Without a command, it reads command lines from standard
input and sends them one at a time.  After a reply code that RFC 3977
follows with a block (LIST, ARTICLE, OVER, LISTGROUP ...) it reads up to
the line holding a single dot.
.PP
With
.BR \-f ,
the lines of
.I file
are sent to the server as they are, without waiting for replies, for
example to feed a prepared IHAVE or POST session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Send the lines of \fIfile\fP instead of a command.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Connect to this port (default 119).
.TP
.B \-v
Also print the command sent and the connect, command and total times.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dclient news.example.com "LIST NEWSGROUPS"
dclient -p 120 localhost "LIST ACTIVE"
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
dreaderd(8),
dreadart(8)
